<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  AncientDangerGenSteps_AmbientDoctrine.xml   UtinniPatches - new 2026-09-10
  ============================================================================
  MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1, piece 2/4. Enforces the ratified ANCIENT column
  (ancient dangers/cryptosleep ruins at map generation) from
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/mechanoid_biome_presence_draft.md.

  VERIFIED before writing (rimsage, 2026-09-10):
  - `BiomeDef.cs`: `public List<GenStepDef> extraGenSteps` and
    `public List<GenStepDef> preventGenSteps` are real fields (both default
    to an empty, already-instantiated List<GenStepDef> - so an empty `[]` in
    the def dump proves nothing about whether the raw XML node exists).
  - The scatterer itself: Core's `BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml` registers
    `GenStepDef defName="ScatterShrines"` (order 750, `genStep Class=
    "GenStep_ScatterShrines"`, `allowInWaterBiome=false`,
    `countPer10kCellsRange` 0.12-0.25) - fires on every player-home map
    (75% skip chance on non-starting maps is in `ShouldSkipMap`, C#, not a
    field). Confirmed live precedent for the exact patch shape: two vanilla-
    adjacent biomes already ship `preventGenSteps: [ScatterShrines]` in the
    current def dump - `ZBiome_Iceberg_NoBeach` and `ZBiome_Sandbar_NoBeach`
    (More Vanilla Biomes) - so `<li>ScatterShrines</li>` inside
    `<preventGenSteps>` is the real, working shape, not invented here.
  - Biome defNames confirmed live/painted the same way as the sibling
    MechClusterBiomes_AmbientDoctrine.xml (against
    `_def_bindings_2026-09-09.md`'s wildAnimals-owner column, cross-checked
    against today's fresh def dump, fingerprint 577/577 matching live
    ModsConfig.xml).
  - `COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Tropical`'s owning mod ships NEITHER
    `preventGenSteps` NOR `extraGenSteps` on either the abstract parent
    `COMIGO_GreaterSwamp` or the concrete child (raw XML read directly,
    `.../3620545124/1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/GreaterSwamps.xml` - no such element
    on either). Unlike the sibling fish patch (which had to target the
    ABSTRACT PARENT for `fishTypes` because patches run before
    `ParentName` inheritance resolves and the field lived only on the
    parent), there is nothing to inherit here - this patch targets the
    CONCRETE CHILD directly and simply creates the field fresh, no
    inheritance-timing trap.

  RARE rows (ExtremeDesert, BiomeGRimond, PoisonForest, BiomeCypreJungle)
  follow the MECHANISM section's own recipe: prevent the stock full-rate
  `ScatterShrines` and add `RUT_ScatterShrinesRare`
  (Defs/MapGeneration/RUT_ScatterShrinesRare.xml, this same commit) - a clone
  with a quartered `countPer10kCellsRange`, documented there.

  ANCIENT=ALLOW rows (the two poles, Scarlands, the Forge, RUT_TheScald,
  Wasteland, AB_TarPits, ZBiome_DesertOasis, ZBiome_Badlands, Desert) get NO
  patch here - default vanilla behaviour already allows the stock genstep,
  and this item's spec does not ask for anything tighter on those rows.
  RUT_TwilightSea/RUT_GreySea (ANCIENT=DENY) are confirmed `isWaterBiome:
  true` in the live def dump - `ScatterShrines`'s own `allowInWaterBiome:
  false` already excludes them, matching the ratified table's own text
  ("the engine already refuses shrine scatter in water biomes...so DENY
  costs nothing") - no patch needed there either.

  Piece 4 (curating shrine CONTENTS where ANCIENT-ALLOW/RARE meets
  AMBIENT-DENY, so a shrine can't wake mechanoid guardians in a biome that
  bans mech clusters) is NOT built here - see the rimflow note on
  MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1: `GenStep_ScatterShrines.ScatterAt` pushes a
  hardcoded symbol ("ancientTemple" -> `SymbolResolver_AncientTemple` ->
  "interior_ancientTemple") through `RimWorld.BaseGen`/`SketchGen`, gated
  only by the GLOBAL `Storyteller.difficulty.peacefulTemples` toggle - no
  per-biome or per-GenStepDef XML field selects guardian type/faction. There
  is no field to patch; doing this for real needs a Harmony postfix on the
  resolver, which is C#, out of this item's XML-only scope.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Alpha Biomes: 6 ANCIENT-DENY rows, prevent only. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <success>Always</success>
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MycoticJungle"]/preventGenSteps</xpath>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MycoticJungle"]</xpath>
            <value><preventGenSteps><li>ScatterShrines</li></preventGenSteps></value>
          </nomatch>
          <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MycoticJungle"]/preventGenSteps</xpath>
            <value><li>ScatterShrines</li></value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_GelatinousSuperorganism"]/preventGenSteps</xpath>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_GelatinousSuperorganism"]</xpath>
            <value><preventGenSteps><li>ScatterShrines</li></preventGenSteps></value>
          </nomatch>
          <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
